## App Output Royalty Clause (1% Fee)

KodrixIDE operates under a success-dependent royalty model for products created within its environment or powered by its integrated engines and runtimes.

### 1. The $50,000 USD Exemption Threshold
You owe absolutely nothing if your product makes a modest amount of money. No royalties are due on the first **$50,000 USD** of gross revenue generated by any single application, game, or digital service built using KodrixIDE. 

### 2. Royalty Obligation
Once a software application, game, or digital product built or compiled using KodrixIDE exceeds **$50,000 USD** in lifetime gross revenue (including sales, subscriptions, advertising, or in-app purchases), you are legally obligated to pay the Licensor a **1% royalty** on all gross revenue generated above that $50,000 mark.

### 3. Reporting and Payment
Users whose products cross the $50,000 USD threshold are required to notify the Licensor within 30 days of the end of the calendar quarter to arrange a royalty distribution structure.

  Contact: @ZohaibBaig144 on X (Twitter)
  GitHub:  https://github.com/Zohaib8090/KodrixIDE

